00:44:13.854 --> 00:44:15.324
and now your book
has the wrong title.

00:44:15.324 --> 00:44:17.454
- Yeah, so amazingly, Rai
Weiss, who won the Nobel Prize

00:44:17.454 --> 00:44:18.824
alongside Kip Thorne
and Barry Barish

00:44:18.824 --> 00:44:20.464
for that discovery, said to me

00:44:20.464 --> 00:44:22.594
about a month before
the detection occurred,

00:44:22.594 --> 00:44:26.094
"If we don't detect black
holes, this thing is a failure."

00:44:26.094 --> 00:44:27.334
And so I got the title,

00:44:27.334 --> 00:44:29.134
really thinking about
Rai saying that.

00:44:29.134 --> 00:44:32.134
That he's now in his 80s, he
started this as a young man,

00:44:32.134 --> 00:44:34.344
and it was the Black Hole Blues,

00:44:34.344 --> 00:44:38.544
but they told me well
before the book came out,

00:44:38.544 --> 00:44:39.474
they told me about
the detection,

00:44:39.474 --> 00:44:40.744
so I didn't wanna re-write it,

00:44:40.744 --> 00:44:42.314
'cause I think it is
all about the pursuit,

00:44:42.314 --> 00:44:44.084
but I did have a lovely close

00:44:44.084 --> 00:44:45.554
where they make the discovery.

00:44:45.554 --> 00:44:46.484
